  data: {
    LLM: "If you hold the Jass (Jack) of trumps, you should almost always 'Take' the bid. 20 points is a massive head start in a 100+ point round.\n\nThe 'Ten' Lead: In plain suits, the 10 is very vulnerable to being captured by an Ace. Only lead a 10 if you have several of that suit or want to draw out the Ace early.\n\nBidding with the Nell: If you hold the Nine of trumps and several other high plain cards, you can bid even without the Jack, provided you can force the Jack to be played on a trick you don't care about.",
    Player: "If you hold the Jass (Jack) of trumps, you should almost always 'Take' the bid. 20 points is a massive head start in a 100+ point round.\n\nThe 'Ten' Lead: In plain suits, the 10 is very vulnerable to being captured by an Ace. Only lead a 10 if you have several of that suit or want to draw out the Ace early.\n\nBidding with the Nell: If you hold the Nine of trumps and several other high plain cards, you can bid even without the Jack, provided you can force the Jack to be played on a trick you don't care about.",
