    basic: "If you hold the Jass (Jack) of trumps, you should almost always 'Take' the bid. 20 points is a massive head start in a 100+ point round.",
    intermediate: "The 'Ten' Lead: In plain suits, the 10 is very vulnerable to being captured by an Ace. Only lead a 10 if you have several of that suit or want to draw out the Ace early.",
    advanced: "Bidding with the Nell: If you hold the Nine of trumps and several other high plain cards, you can bid even without the Jack, provided you can force the Jack to be played on a trick you don't care about.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Always announce 'Bella' when playing your King or Queen of trumps! Forgetting the call loses the 20-point bonus.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "The 7 of Trumps (The 'Seven of Diamonds' in many traditions) can be swapped for the face-up card if it was the trump-setter.",
      },
